    "title": "pandas.Index.name — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1386.gcb2086a1a4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Index.name#\n\n- property Index.name[source]#\n- Return Index or MultiIndex name. The name (or label) of an Index provides metadata that can be used to identify the axis in DataFrames and Series. \n  - Returns:\n    - label (hashable object)\n    - The name of the Index.\n See also \n  - `Index.set_names`\n  - Able to set new names partially and by level.\n  - `Index.rename`\n  - Able to set new names partially and by level.\n  - `Series.name`\n  - Corresponding Series property.\n Examples >>> idx = pd.Index([1, 2, 3], name=\"x\") >>> idx Index([1, 2, 3], dtype='int64', name='x') >>> idx.name 'x'",
    "markdown_length": 596,
